message: "If you use these exercises or their fixtures in a course, a paper or a syllabus, please cite them as below."
title: "Tennis API exercises: graded coding exercises for a real JSON API"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
authors:
  - name: "Live Tennis API"
    website: "https://livetennisapi.com"
    email: "hello@livetennisapi.com"
repository-code: "https://gitlab.com/livetennisapi/tennis-api-exercises"
url: "https://docs.livetennisapi.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Eight graded exercises in Python and JavaScript that teach students to call
  a real JSON API, read nested data, handle errors and rate limits, and stay
  inside a daily request quota. Tests run offline against recorded responses
  from the free plan of Live Tennis API. Code is MIT. Fixtures are CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - teaching
  - programming exercises
  - REST API
  - JSON
  - Python
  - JavaScript
  - tennis
  - sports data
